{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0040","statement":"The Flickr30K dataset is a collection of over 30,000 images with 5 crowdsourced descriptions each.","source_span":"a collection of over 30,000 images with 5 crowdsourced descriptions each"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0040","statement":"Hodosh et al. (2013, p. 859) claim the crowdsourced descriptions focus only on the information that can be obtained from the image alone.","source_span":"focus only on the information that can be obtained from the image alone"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0040","statement":"The Flickr8K dataset is a subset of the Flickr30K dataset.","source_span":"about the Flickr8K dataset, a subset of Flickr30K"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0040","statement":"beukeboom2014mechanisms defines linguistic bias as a systematic asymmetry in word choice as a function of the social category to which the target belongs.","source_span":"a systematic asymmetry in word choice as a function of the social category to which the target belongs"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0040","statement":"The author distinguishes two kinds of verbal behavior resulting from stereotypes: linguistic bias and unwarranted inferences.","source_span":"(i) linguistic bias, and (ii) unwarranted inferences"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0040","statement":"The author grouped unwarranted inferences found in a subset of the Flickr30K data into six categories.","source_span":"I have grouped these inferences into six categories"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0040","statement":"In image 2659046789, an annotator wrote 'A little boy is eating pie without utensils,' revealing the belief that pie should be eaten with utensils.","source_span":"A little boy is eating pie without utensils (image 2659046789)"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0040","statement":"In image 8063007, a description says the 'manager' was talking about job performance and scolding a worker in a stern lecture.","source_span":"talking about job performance and scolding [a worker] in a stern lecture (8063007)"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0040","statement":"In image 4280272, dark-skinned individuals are called African-American regardless of whether the picture was taken in the USA.","source_span":"Many dark-skinned individuals are called African-American regardless of whether the picture has been taken in the USA or not (4280272)"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0040","statement":"In image 4183120, people sitting at a gym are described as watching a game, even though there could be any sort of event going on.","source_span":"people sitting at a gym are said to be watching a game, even though there could be any sort of event going on"}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0040","fact_refs":[0],"question":"How many images does the Flickr30K dataset contain, and how many crowdsourced descriptions does each image have?","answer":"The Flickr30K dataset contains over 30,000 images, each with 5 crowdsourced descriptions."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0040","fact_refs":[1],"question":"According to Hodosh et al. (2013), what do the crowdsourced descriptions in datasets like Flickr30K supposedly focus on?","answer":"They are assumed to focus only on the information that can be obtained from the image alone."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0040","fact_refs":[2],"question":"What is the relationship between the Flickr8K and Flickr30K datasets?","answer":"Flickr8K is a subset of the Flickr30K dataset."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0040","fact_refs":[3],"question":"How does beukeboom2014mechanisms define linguistic bias?","answer":"As a systematic asymmetry in word choice as a function of the social category to which the target belongs."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0040","fact_refs":[4],"question":"What two types of verbal behavior resulting from stereotypes does the paper distinguish?","answer":"Linguistic bias and unwarranted inferences."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0040","fact_refs":[6],"question":"What belief does the annotator's description of image 2659046789 ('A little boy is eating pie without utensils') reveal?","answer":"It reveals the annotator's normative belief that pie should be eaten with utensils."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0041","statement":"The paper investigates two neural network architectures for relation classification: convolutional neural networks (CNNs) and recurrent neural networks (RNNs).","source_span":"investigates two different neural architectures for the task of relation classification: convolutional neural networks and recurrent neural networks"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0041","statement":"The proposed neural models achieve state-of-the-art results on the SemEval 2010 relation classification task.","source_span":"Our neural models achieve state-of-the-art results on the SemEval 2010 relation classification task."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0041","statement":"The example sentence 'We poured the milk into the pumpkin mixture' expresses the relation Entity-Destination(e1,e2).","source_span":"expresses the relation Entity-Destination(e1,e2)"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0041","statement":"The extended middle context combines (1) the left context, left entity, and middle context, and (2) the middle context, right entity, and right context.","source_span":"a combination of the left context, the left entity and the middle context; and (2) a combination of the middle context, the right entity and the right context"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0041","statement":"deSantos2015 replaced the softmax layer of the CNN with a ranking layer and published the best result so far on the SemEval dataset, to the authors' knowledge.","source_span":"deSantos2015 replaced the softmax layer of the CNN with a ranking layer. They showed improvements and published the best result so far on the SemEval dataset"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0041","statement":"The example sentence 'He had chest pain and headaches from mold in the bedroom' is used to show the model can detect the relation Cause-Effect(e2,e1).","source_span":"the model can detect the relation Cause-Effect(e2,e1)"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0041","statement":"The convolutional layer applies 2D filters with different window sizes from 2 to 5 (multi-windows).","source_span":"We apply filters with different window sizes 2-5 (multi-windows)"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0041","statement":"Manually annotated relation classification data was released in 2010 as part of a SemEval shared task.","source_span":"In 2010, manually annotated data for relation classification was released in the context of a SemEval shared task"}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0041","fact_refs":[0],"question":"What two types of neural network architectures does this paper investigate for relation classification?","answer":"Convolutional neural networks (CNNs) and recurrent neural networks (RNNs)."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0041","fact_refs":[2],"question":"What relation does the example sentence 'We poured the milk into the pumpkin mixture' express?","answer":"It expresses the relation Entity-Destination(e1,e2)."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0041","fact_refs":[3],"question":"What are the two context combinations used in the paper's 'extended middle context' representation for CNNs?","answer":"(1) the left context, left entity, and middle context, and (2) the middle context, right entity, and right context."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0041","fact_refs":[4],"question":"What change did deSantos2015 make to the CNN architecture for relation classification, and what was the result?","answer":"They replaced the softmax layer with a ranking layer, achieving the best published result on the SemEval dataset at the time."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0041","fact_refs":[6],"question":"What window sizes are used for the convolutional filters in the CNN model described in the paper?","answer":"Window sizes 2 to 5 (multi-windows)."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0041","fact_refs":[7],"question":"In what year was manually annotated relation classification data released via a SemEval shared task?","answer":"In 2010."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0042","statement":"The paper's goal-oriented dialog tasks are set in the context of restaurant reservation and require manipulating sentences and symbols to conduct conversations, issue API calls, and use their outputs.","source_span":"Set in the context of restaurant reservation, our tasks require manipulating sentences and symbols, so as to properly conduct conversations, issue API calls and use the outputs of such calls."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0042","statement":"An end-to-end dialog system based on Memory Networks can reach promising, yet imperfect, performance on the tasks.","source_span":"an end-to-end dialog system based on Memory Networks can reach promising, yet imperfect, performance and learn to perform non-trivial operations"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0042","statement":"The results are confirmed by comparing the system to a hand-crafted slot-filling baseline on data from the second Dialog State Tracking Challenge (Henderson et al., 2014a).","source_span":"comparing our system to a hand-crafted slot-filling baseline on data from the second Dialog State Tracking Challenge (Henderson et al., 2014a)"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0042","statement":"The first five restaurant reservation tasks are generated by a simulation, and the last one uses real human-bot dialogs.","source_span":"The first five tasks are generated by a simulation, the last one uses real human-bot dialogs."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0042","statement":"The data for all the restaurant reservation dialog tasks is available at http://fb.ai/babi.","source_span":"The data for all tasks is available at http://fb.ai/babi."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0042","statement":"The authors also give results on a proprietary dataset extracted from an online restaurant reservation concierge service with anonymized users.","source_span":"a proprietary dataset extracted from an online restaurant reservation concierge service with anonymized users"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0042","statement":"The authors thank Martin Raison, Alex Lebrun, and Laurent Landowski for their help with the Concierge data.","source_span":"The authors would like to thank Martin Raison, Alex Lebrun and Laurent Landowski for their help with the Concierge data."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0042","fact_refs":[0],"question":"What is the setting for the goal-oriented dialog tasks proposed in this paper?","answer":"They are set in the context of restaurant reservation, requiring manipulating sentences and symbols to conduct conversations, issue API calls, and use the outputs of those calls."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0042","fact_refs":[1],"question":"What kind of dialog system does the paper show can reach promising but imperfect performance on the restaurant reservation tasks?","answer":"An end-to-end dialog system based on Memory Networks."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0042","fact_refs":[2],"question":"What baseline is the Memory Network system compared against, and on what data?","answer":"A hand-crafted slot-filling baseline, evaluated on data from the second Dialog State Tracking Challenge (Henderson et al., 2014a)."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0042","fact_refs":[3],"question":"How were the first five restaurant reservation tasks created, and how was the sixth one obtained?","answer":"The first five tasks were generated by simulation, while the last one uses real human-bot dialogs."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0042","fact_refs":[4],"question":"Where can the data for the restaurant reservation dialog tasks be found?","answer":"At http://fb.ai/babi."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0042","fact_refs":[6],"question":"Who did the authors thank for their help with the Concierge data?","answer":"Martin Raison, Alex Lebrun, and Laurent Landowski."}
